# NewUnera — Custom dropdown (no native `<select>`)

For user-facing option pickers in modals, filters, steppers, and forms under `NewUnera/`, **do not** use `<select class="form-select">`. Use the **add-money currency dropdown** pattern instead.

## Forbidden

- `<select class="form-select">` (or any native `<select>`) for visible option lists
- Storing the chosen value only on the toggle button (must use a hidden input)
- CSS gradient functions on dropdown chrome (see `new-brand-output.mdc`)

## Required DOM structure

```html
<div class="dropdown"><!-- optional: payee-dropdown, currency-selector -->
  <button type="button" class="dropdown-toggle" id="…Toggle"
          aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false" aria-labelledby="…Label">
    <span class="selected-currency" id="…Display">
      <span class="currency-flag" aria-hidden="true">🇨🇦</span>
      <span>
        <div class="currency-code">CAD</div>
        <div class="currency-name">Canadian Dollar</div>
      </span>
    </span>
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 -960 960 960"
         fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M480-345 240-585l56-56 184 184 184-184 56 56-240 240Z"/></svg>
  </button>
  <div class="dropdown-menu" id="…Menu" role="listbox" aria-label="…">
    <div class="dropdown-list" id="…List">
      <div class="dropdown-item" role="option" tabindex="0" data-value="CAD">…</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <input type="hidden" id="…" name="…" value="CAD" required>
</div>
```

## Sizing and tokens

| Element | Spec |
|--------|------|
| `.dropdown-toggle` | `height: 52px`, full width in modals, `border: 2px solid var(--border-subtle)` |
| Focus | `outline: 2px solid var(--brand-deep-blue); outline-offset: 2px` on toggle and `.dropdown-item` |
| Chevron | Rotates when `aria-expanded="true"`; `fill="currentColor"` Material path (see canonical) |
| Value storage | `<input type="hidden">` with stable `id` / `name` for submit handlers |

Use **flag + code + name** in toggle and items (`.currency-flag`, `.currency-code`, `.currency-name`). Fiat lists use **CAD / USD / EUR / GBP** codes (not `hCAD`) unless the screen is explicitly HUMA-token scoped.

## Search row

Include `.dropdown-search` only when option count is **greater than ~5**. For ≤5 options (network, card type, short fiat lists), omit search.

